name issue_124_burst_loss_v2
describe 3% loss in bursts of ~6 packets, 2 Mbps, every v2 switch on: the flip's burst_loss cell next to libwebrtc (issue #124)
# `burst_loss` with the configuration PR #116 makes the default. Measured on main 74266b3, seeds 1-10 (ours / libwebrtc, parity-data of main):
#   cc.queue_p95_ms 45-108 (mean 73.5) / 46.8 ; video.e2e_delay_p95_ms 188-241 (mean 210.7) / 213.0
#   cc.utilization_pct 81.1-87.0 (mean 84.0) / 80.4 ; cc.target_avg_kbps 1787 / 1757 ; video.freeze_total_ms 640 / 1433
# Left: the queue p95 is 27 ms above libwebrtc's mean (the same excess shows on bufferbloat); the lines below lock the level reached.
# Target (issue #124): cc.queue_p95_ms within the parity band of libwebrtc (46.8 ms).
cc v2
pacer v2
tcc v2
rtx v2
rtcp v2
keyframe v2
allocator v2
packetization v2
audio v2
duration 30s
at 0s capacity=2000kbps delay=50ms loss=3% burst=6 queue=300ms
expect audio.concealed_pct < 5
expect audio.interruptions <= 1
expect video.longest_freeze_ms < 1200
expect video.render_fps >= 25
expect cc.queue_p95_ms < 120
expect video.e2e_delay_p95_ms < 260
expect cc.utilization_pct >= 78
